---
The **Delete Lead** action allows you to permanently remove a lead that is no longer relevant or needed in your system.

## When to Use

Delete a lead when:

- The lead is no longer valid or relevant
- It is a duplicate entry
- The lead has been incorrectly created
- It will not be converted or pursued

## How to Delete a Lead

1. Go to **Taskip > Leads**.
1. Find the lead you want to delete.
1. Click the **three-dot menu (⋯)** on the right side of the lead
1. Select **Delete Lead**

![](./delete-a-lead/content/image.png)

Before deletion, the system will ask for confirmation to prevent accidental removal.

## Important Notes

- Deleting a lead is **permanent and cannot be undone**
- All associated data (notes, files, history) will be removed
- This action should be used with caution

## Best Practices

- Double-check before deleting a lead
- Use filters to identify duplicates instead of deleting blindly
- Consider converting or archiving leads before deletion (if needed)
